{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_StandardSolution#Restim","title":"Restim","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_StandardSolution.md","line":790,"body":"","kind":"proof","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_StandardSolution.tex#Restim","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_StandardSolution#thm:standard-solution-canonical-neighborhoods]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_BasicsOfRicciFlow#lem:distance-nonincreasing]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch11_GeometricLimits#controlnbhd]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_KappaAncientSolutions#canonvary]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#narrows]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch11_GeometricLimits#omega]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch11_GeometricLimits#kaplimit]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_KappaAncientSolutions#asympvol]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#thm:bishop-gromov]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_StandardSolution.tex","label":"Restim","line":574,"source":"\\label{Restim}\n\nThere is $c>0$ such that $R(p,t)\\ge c/(1-t)$ everywhere.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\uses{thm:standard-solution-canonical-neighborhoods,lem:distance-nonincreasing,controlnbhd,canonvary,narrows,omega,kaplimit,asympvol,thm:bishop-gromov}\n\\sketch A global metric limit at time $1$ would produce arbitrarily small\ncanonical necks, contradicting the narrow-neck estimate. A point with bounded\ncurvature would likewise contradict the zero asymptotic volume of a blowup\n$\\kappa$-solution and Bishop--Gromov. Canonical-neighborhood derivative\ncontrol then integrates to the stated uniform lower bound.\n\\end{proof}\n\n\\begin{theorem}[Trichotomy of canonical neighborhoods in the standard solution]","html":" <p></p><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-52657374696d\"></span> <p></p>There is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c&gt;0$\">$c&gt;0$</span> such that <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$R(p,t)\\ge c/(1-t)$\">$R(p,t)\\ge c/(1-t)$</span> everywhere.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh12_StandardSolution%23thm%3Astandard-solution-canonical-neighborhoods\">↗ thm:standard-solution-canonical-neighborhoods</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_BasicsOfRicciFlow%23lem%3Adistance-nonincreasing\">↗ lem:distance-nonincreasing</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh11_GeometricLimits%23controlnbhd\">↗ controlnbhd</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_KappaAncientSolutions%23canonvary\">↗ canonvary</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23narrows\">↗ narrows</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh11_GeometricLimits%23omega\">↗ omega</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh11_GeometricLimits%23kaplimit\">↗ kaplimit</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_KappaAncientSolutions%23asympvol\">↗ asympvol</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23thm%3Abishop-gromov\">↗ thm:bishop-gromov</a> \\sketch A global metric limit at time <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1$\">$1$</span> would produce arbitrarily small canonical necks, contradicting the narrow-neck estimate. A point with bounded curvature would likewise contradict the zero asymptotic volume of a blowup <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\kappa $\">$\\kappa $</span>-solution and Bishop–Gromov. Canonical-neighborhood derivative control then integrates to the stated uniform lower bound. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section> <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section>[Trichotomy of canonical neighborhoods in the standard solution]","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_StandardSolution#prop:standard-solution-scalar-curvature-lower-bound","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_StandardSolution#thm:standard-solution-trichotomy","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_StandardSolution#thm:standard-solution-canonical-neighborhoods","title":"thm:standard-solution-canonical-neighborhoods","label":"thm:standard-solution-canonical-neighborhoods"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_BasicsOfRicciFlow#lem:distance-nonincreasing","title":"lem:distance-nonincreasing","label":"lem:distance-nonincreasing"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch11_GeometricLimits#controlnbhd","title":"controlnbhd","label":"controlnbhd"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_KappaAncientSolutions#canonvary","title":"canonvary","label":"canonvary"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#narrows","title":"narrows","label":"narrows"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch11_GeometricLimits#omega","title":"o